vey and the ratings consensus, landing at a modest Republican edge.", "watch": "Any independent, non-partisan polling in the final week confirming or contradicting the Democratic internal would move this materially.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Turner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Mike Turner, a longtime Republican incumbent, faces Democrat Kristina Knickerbocker in a Dayton-area district that leans Republican by about four points. The race has drawn heavy outside spending, and Ohio Democrats have outraised Republicans in the home stretch, with analysts increasingly rating long-safe Ohio seats as competitive. Knickerbocker has raised over a million dollars, though Turner holds a cash advantage.\n\nMost expert ratings call the race Lean R, with a few at Likely R and one at Tossup. A Democratic-sponsored poll from mid-October showed Knickerbocker narrowly ahead, while earlier summer surveys had Turner up by six to seven. Prediction markets give Turner roughly a two-in-three chance. The balance of evidence points to a narrow Republican advantage with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1787, "margin": -5.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1387, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1203, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.119, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1452, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1169, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1476, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1448, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1049, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1332, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1191, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-